  "thig12.1:1.2": "Norman and Ṭhānissaro, evidently under the influence of the commentary, translate in present tense, but <i lang='pi' translate='no'>udakamotariṁ</i> is an aorist in past tense, as is rendered by Mahendra. If the commentary is correct, she is telling a story from before she ordained. But both the brahmin’s respectful form of addresses (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>bhoti</i>) and the boldness of her teachings suggest she was already a nun. ",
  "thig12.1:1.3": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Ayyānaṁ</i> is ambiguous; it could be either male or female. ",
