  "thig12.1:6.3": "Here, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>nāga</i> cannot be cobra or elephant, so it must be the supernatural creature, which is said to live in underwater lairs. | <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Susumāra</i> (literally “child-killer”) may be either the Gangetic dolphin (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn129/en/sujato#21.3'>MN 129:21.3</a>) or the crocodile (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/cp27/en/sujato#1.3'>Cp 27:1.3</a>). The dolphin is more obviously a “water-dweller”. ",
